Overall assessment (brief)
PSEG is a well‑resourced, regulated utility that has moved decisively from merchant fossil assets to an infrastructure‑driven, clean‑energy orientation. The company has deployed multiple sustainable technologies at operational scale (AMI, large energy‑efficiency programs, widespread EV make‑ready and charger deployment, grid modernization), run pilots in hydrogen and storage, and produced clearly measurable emissions and customer savings. Its strengths are program scale, regulated investment capacity, and reliable carbon‑free baseload (nuclear). Its innovation posture is solid — many pilots, partnerships and regulatory demonstrations — but much activity remains pilot or third‑party project based rather than dominated by PSEG‑owned, breakthrough technology platforms at multi‑GW scale. The final score (80/100) reflects strong adoption and measurable results, with room to grow in proprietary breakthrough tech and in owning/operating larger battery and hydrogen systems at scale relative to the most aggressive national peers.

